  DOES THE INSTRUMENT RANK STRUCTURE ABOVE JITTER?
    3 Hz rhythm (the FRAME)   13.00
    moving formants (CONTENT) 1.27
    held vowel                0.89
    the creature              13.52

  salience REFUSES ITSELF -- a real 3 Hz amplitude rhythm scores 13.00
  against the creature's 13.52. The measure ranks a jittery drone at or
  above the structure the reward exists to find, so it is reading JITTER
  (noise_amp 0.28, vocal parameters fluctuating every tick) and not
  spectrotemporal structure. The headroom below is headroom in noise.
  Warlaumont's salience runs through Coath & Denham's cortical filtering
  and edge detection; a raw frame-to-frame difference is not that, and
  this is where the simplification fails.
